{
  "$comment": [
    "MEASURED against production (project ixvwfbuvfxxsjiywhbbb) on 2026-08-19, not derived",
    "from supabase/migrations/. Those files describe a different lineage than the live",
    "database (see docs/DB-HARDENING-AUDIT.md), so the catalog is the only honest source.",
    "Re-measure with `node scripts/check-rls.mjs`, or with the SQL in docs/AUTH-MODEL.md.",
    "src/lib/auth/rls-manifest.test.ts is the CI gate that reads this file."
  ],
  "measured_at": "2026-09-07",
  "reverified_at": "2026-09-07",
  "$reverified_comment": [
    "Re-measured against production on 2026-09-07 through the Supabase MCP, read only,",
    "with the query scripts/check-rls.mjs --sql prints. 53 tables became 71: eighteen",
    "arrived with migrations applied since 2026-08-19 (refunds, reviews, wishlists,",
    "subscriptions and its charges, the four report_* rollups, supplier_branches,",
    "search_index_outbox, payout_statements and its lines, and the rest).",
    "RLS is on for all 71 and every one of them now has at least one policy.",
    "",
    "THE EIGHT ZERO-POLICY TABLES ARE NO LONGER ZERO-POLICY, and that is 122 landing,",
    "not a loosening: seven carry `deny_all_client_roles`, RESTRICTIVE, ALL commands,",
    "anon+authenticated, USING false WITH CHECK false. Deny-by-default is now stated",
    "instead of implied, so `client_locked` below records the LOCK rather than a count.",
    "",
    "payment_webhook_events is the one real change: it now carries a PERMISSIVE SELECT",
    "for authenticated where is_admin(), so an admin can read the webhook journal. It",
    "is therefore not client-locked any more and has moved out of the list."
  ],
  "project_ref": "ixvwfbuvfxxsjiywhbbb",
